  "log": [
    "====================================================================================================",
    "DISTOGRAM OF EVERY RANKING ARM -- does a summary statistic hide a local signal?",
    "====================================================================================================",
    "  Spearman is global and monotonic; top-k needs the answer to beat 2,400 rivals. Both can miss an",
    "  arm that separates near-native from decoys non-monotonically. This asks that directly, as AUC.",
    "  AUC_far   = near-native (<=5 A) vs far (>10 A)   -- the easy separation",
    "  AUC_close = near-native (<=5 A) vs close-wrong (5-10 A) -- the one a funnel needs",
    "  PREDECLARED: AUC_close >= 0.65 with Spearman ~0 => the statistic hid a usable detector.",
    "  AUC_close ~ 0.5 everywhere => the nulls stand and the distogram explains why.",
    "  AUC_far high but AUC_close ~ 0.5 => the arms only reject absurd poses, which the clash filter",
    "  already does -- that would explain every result to date in one sentence.",
